],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, October to November is the driest pair on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, with a normal of 6.36 inches, and it came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years since 1951. In 2025 that pair ran 41% of normal on the middle of the grids, and November to December ran 34%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 30% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 18198 had its driest year in 2007, at 62% of normal.</p>"}
